# Scribble Lab — Technical Plan

## Findings
The starter has a working room create/join/fetch flow with in-memory storage but implements zero game logic. The frontend has a complete UI shell with placeholder components for all game features. The API base URL has a typo (`/bug` instead of no path).

## State Model Changes

### Backend — `Room` (src/models/game.ts)
```typescript
// New fields to add:
RoomStatus = "lobby" | "playing" | "roundEnd"

interface Room {
  // existing...
  hostId: string;              // participantId of the host
  status: RoomStatus;
  currentDrawerId: string | null;
  currentWord: string | null;
  guesses: Guess[];            // all guesses this round
  scores: Record<string, number>;  // participantId -> score
  canvasData: string;          // serialized drawing strokes (JSON)
}

interface Guess {
  participantId: string;
  text: string;
  correct: boolean;
  timestamp: string;
}

// RoomSnapshot updated to include:
// - hostId, currentDrawerId, currentWord (null for guessers), scores, guesses, canvasData, status
```

### Frontend — `RoomSnapshot` (src/services/api.ts)
```typescript
// Match backend model additions:
status: "lobby" | "playing" | "roundEnd";
hostId: string;
currentDrawerId: string | null;
currentWord: string | null;
scores: Record<string, number>;
guesses: Array<{ participantId: string; text: string; correct: boolean; timestamp: string }>;
canvasData: string;
```

## Data Flow

### Lobby Flow
1. Frontend polls `GET /rooms/:code?participantId=...` every 2s.
2. Backend returns room snapshot (participants, hostId, status).
3. Frontend checks if status changed to `"playing"` → auto-navigate to `/game`.

### Game Start Flow
1. Host clicks "Start Game" → `POST /rooms/:code/start`.
2. Backend: sets drawer (first participant), selects word (deterministic index), sets status to `"playing"`.
3. All clients detect `status === "playing"` on next poll → show GamePage.

### Drawing Flow
1. Drawer draws on canvas → strokes serialized as JSON array.
2. On each stroke (debounced) → `POST /rooms/:code/draw` with `{ strokes }`.
3. Backend stores `canvasData`.
4. Guessers poll `GET /rooms/:code` and render canvas from `canvasData`.

### Guess Flow
1. Guesser submits guess → `POST /rooms/:code/guess` with `{ text }`.
2. Backend trims, case-insensitively compares to `currentWord`.
3. If correct: sets `correct: true`, awards 100 points, sets status to `"roundEnd"`.
4. If incorrect: appends guess with `correct: false`, 0 points.
5. All players see updated guess history and scores via polling.

### Restart Flow
1. Host clicks "Restart" → `POST /rooms/:code/restart`.
2. Backend clears `currentDrawerId`, `currentWord`, `guesses`, `scores`, `canvasData`, sets status to `"lobby"`.
3. All clients detect `status === "lobby"` on next poll → navigate to `/lobby`.

## File-Level Plan

### Backend Changes
| File | Changes |
|------|---------|
| `src/models/game.ts` | Add `hostId`, `Guess` type, new statuses, scores, canvasData to Room |
| `src/api/schemas.ts` | Add schemas for `startGameParams`, `submitGuessBody`, `drawBody` |
| `src/services/roomStore.ts` | Add `startGame`, `submitGuess`, `saveDraw`, `restartGame` methods; update `toRoomSnapshot` for viewer context |
| `src/api/rooms.ts` | Add `POST /:code/start`, `POST /:code/guess`, `POST /:code/draw`, `POST /:code/restart` handlers |
| `src/api/router.ts` | Register new routes (no changes needed if using router prefix) |

### Frontend Changes
| File | Changes |
|------|---------|
| `src/services/api.ts` | Fix `/bug` typo; add `startGame`, `submitGuess`, `saveDraw`, `restartGame` methods; update types |
| `src/state/roomStore.ts` | Add `startGame`, `submitGuess`, `restartGame` methods |
| `src/pages/LobbyPage.tsx` | Add auto-polling (~2s); only host sees Start button; disable if <2 players; navigate on game start |
| `src/pages/GamePage.tsx` | Add role-aware rendering: drawer sees canvas + word, guessers see canvas + guess form; add polling; handle roundEnd/result state |
| `src/components/GuessForm.tsx` | Connect to API; add validation; disable for drawer |
| `src/components/Scoreboard.tsx` | Render dynamic scores from snapshot |
| `src/components/ResultPanel.tsx` | Show final word, scores, guess history; host sees Restart button |

## Implementation Sequence
1. Fix `/bug` typo in `api.ts`
2. Update state model (types, schemas)
3. Add backend endpoints (start, guess, draw, restart)
4. Add lobby polling + host controls
5. Implement canvas drawing (drawer) + canvas display (guessers)
6. Implement guess submission + validation
7. Implement scoring + guess history sync
8. Implement result state + restart
9. Validation: test with two browser tabs

## Testing Strategy
- Manual testing with two browser tabs for all four scenarios.
- Existing unit tests must continue to pass.
- Run `npm run build` in both frontend and backend after each phase.

## Risks
- Canvas drawing sync via polling may feel laggy — acceptable per spec (no WebSockets).
- Determistic word selection means same room always picks first word — acceptable for lab scope.
- In-memory state means server restart loses all rooms — acceptable per spec.
